ts, no imitation","text":"rl-v2 tests whether the GA genome is a head start or a ceiling: same network, inputs and PPO as rl-v1, only the start changes. Self-play first, then the bots, then every earlier model.","rejected":"Imitation first (that is rl-v1); a new architecture (would mix two changes into one comparison)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Stage 1 ends on a plateau, not a score","text":"The first start ended self-play after 12 iterations, when it beat the bots 50% of the time. Self-play is the point of the project, so stage 1 now runs until the score against the GA genome has not improved for 60 iterations (at most 400): it shows how far self-play gets alone.","rejected":"A fixed bots threshold (ended the stage after 3 minutes); a fixed iteration count (could stop while it is still learning, or waste hours on a plateau)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"1,500 games per iteration","text":"Random players make long games with ~210 decisions each; 3,000 of them (rl-v1's setting) ran the 8 GB laptop out of memory. 1,500 fit with room for the evaluation.","rejected":"Keeping 3,000 with float16 features (a change to the shared code that rl-v1 does not have)."},{"t":"2026-11-18 13:16:01","kind":"decision","title":"Same evaluation games as rl-v1","text":"The per-iteration evaluation and the goal checks use rl-v1's and az-v1's seeds, so every number compares directly with them. A new confirmation seed is kept for the end.","rejected":"New evaluation seeds (no direct comparison)."}],"reports":[],"strip":{"alive":true,"run":"z1","stage":"3","goal_text":"82.8%","stages_text":"2 of 3 stages passed","best_text":"74.1%","verified_text":"73.0%","verified_sub":"z1 iteration 1000, n=1000"}}